cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "AnnotateR"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Das
    given-names: Jyotirmoy
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5649-4658"
  - family-names: Volpe
    given-names: Massimiliano
repository-code: "https://github.com/pyrevo/annotater"
description: >-
  Genomic coordinate annotation tool: annotate query coordinates
  (BED/VCF/tabular) against annotation features (GFF/GTF/BED/tabular)
  with a Streamlit interface. Bedtools and Polars-Bio are interchangeable
  execution backends producing identical canonical results for overlap,
  contains, within, and closest matching, with optional minimum-overlap
  and strand-aware filtering.
keywords:
  - genomics
  - interval annotation
  - bedtools
  - polars-bio
  - streamlit
# NOTE: the `license` field is intentionally omitted until the repository
# license is settled: LICENSE is BSD-3-Clause while README.md and the app
# footer state GPLv3 (see docs/implementation-notes.md, Task 8 release
# audit). Do not add a value here without resolving that discrepancy.